and SMTP settings so email can be delivered and return users to the website.",Tbe="Email confirmation cannot be enabled yet. Complete: {items}",Pbe="This email feature cannot be enabled yet. Complete: {items}",kbe="Configure URL",Abe="Configure SMTP",Rbe="Magic link and email OTP",Dbe="Allow passwordless sign-in by emailed link or one-time passcode. Turning this off disables both flows.",xbe="Email delivery",Lbe="Authentication email is delivered through this project's own SMTP server.",Obe="SMTP host",Nbe="smtp.example.com",Mbe="SMTP port",Fbe="Minimum interval per user (seconds)",jbe="Minimum time between authentication emails to the same user. The official default is 60 seconds.",Bbe="Project email limit per hour",Ube="Maximum authentication emails this project can send per hour. Use 0 to disable authentication email. The official custom SMTP default is 30.",$be="SMTP username",Vbe="SMTP password",Gbe="Enter the SMTP password",Hbe="Leave blank to keep the saved password",Wbe="The password is encrypted when saved and is never returned to the browser.",Qbe="Sender email",qbe="no-reply{'@'}example.com",zbe="TLS mode",Kbe="TLS is selected automatically: port 465 uses implicit TLS; other ports use STARTTLS.",Ybe="Enabled",Jbe="Disabled",Zbe="Site URL",Xbe="Allowed redirect URLs",e2e="Not configured",t2e="{count} configured",n2e="Configuration version",s2e="Email authentication settings",o2e="Prepare the next email sign-up configuration without changing the live website.",i2e="Draft only — no live changes",a2e="Sender name",r2e="Readdy",l2e="Shown as the sender name in recipients' inboxes. It takes effect only after this draft is activated.",c2e="Send a test email",d2e="Use the saved draft or active configuration to verify DNS, TLS, credentials, and sender permissions.",u2e="Recipient for the test email",p2e="Send Test Email",h2e="Sending…",f2e="Save the current SMTP settings before sending a test email.",m2e="Enter a valid recipient and save the SMTP settings first.",g2e="Test email sent. Check the recipient inbox.",y2e="SMTP test failed. Check the host, port, credentials, sender address, and provider permissions.",v2e="https://www.example.com",b2e="The default destination after a visitor completes authentication.",w2e="https://www.example.com/auth/callback",S2e="Enter one callback per line. HTTPS, HTTP, wildcards, mobile app schemes, and Chrome extension URLs are supported.",_2e="Discard Changes",C2e="Save Draft",I2e="Saving…",E2e="Authentication draft saved. The live website is unchanged.",T2e="Authentication draft couldn't be saved. Try again.",P2e="Release and activate email authentication",k2e="Complete the compatibility steps before changing how the published website authenticates visitors.",A2e="Regenerate the website's authentication flow",R2e="Ask Readdy to add the confirmation callback, pending-verification state, and resend action while preserving the existing sign-in experience.",D2e="Copy Regeneration Request",x2e="Open Editor",L2e="Regeneration request copied.",O2e="The regeneration request couldn't be copied. Try again.",N2e="Review and publish the generated changes",M2e="Test sign-up and sign-in in preview, then publish the compatible website before activating this configuration.",F2e="Open Publish Settings",j2e="Confirm the compatible website is live",B2e="Activation is unlocked only after you confirm the regenerated authentication flow has been published.",U2e="I regenerated, tested, and published the compatible authentication flow.",$2e="No compatibility release is required",V2e="This draft does not newly enable email confirmation or magic links, so it can be activated after review.",G2e="Save or discard your current edits before activation. Unsaved changes are never activated.",H2e="Complete the URL configuration and, when email is enabled, the SMTP settings before activation.",W2e="Discard Saved Draft",Q2e="Discard the saved draft?",q2e="Only the draft will be removed. The currently active or legacy authentication behavior will remain unchanged.",z2e="Discard Draft",K2e="The saved draft was discarded. Live authentication is unchanged.",Y2e="The saved draft couldn't be discarded. Live authentication is unchanged.",J2e="Activate Email Configuration",Z2e="Enhanced authentication is active",X2e="The configuration is live. Authentication services may take up to 30 seconds to refresh.",e5e="Restore Original Defaults",t5e="Activate this email authentication configuration?",n5e="The saved draft will become live and authentication services may take up to 30 seconds to refresh. If activation fails, the previous active behavior stays unchanged.",s5e="Cancel",o5e="Activate",i5e="Activating…",a5e="Authentication configuration activated. Allow up to 30 seconds for all services to refresh.",r5e="Activation failed. The previous active authentication behavior remains unchanged.",l5e="Restore the original authentication defaults?",c5e="This removes the enhanced draft and active configuration, disables Google sign-in while keeping its credentials, and returns the project to its original authentication defaults.",d5e="Restore Original Defaults",u5e="Restoring…",p5e="The original authentication defaults have been restored.",h5e="The original defaults couldn't be restored. The current authentication configuration remains unchanged.",f5e="You can review these settings, but only the project owner can save, test, activate, restore, or change provider credentials.",m5e="Update this generated website's authentication flow without removing existing behavior. Add /auth/callback handling for email confirmation and magic-link callbacks; show a pending-email-verification state after sign-up; provide an action to resend the confirmation email; complete the magic-link session; and preserve existing sign-in, sign-up, and session logic. Never expose service-role or SMTP credentials in frontend code.",g5e="Update this generated website's email-confirmation flow without removing existing behavior. Add /auth/callback handling for email-confirmation callbacks; show a pending-email-verification state after sign-up; provide an action to resend the confirmation email; and preserve existing sign-in, sign-up, and session logic. Never expose service-role or SMTP credentials in frontend code.",y5e="Update this generated website's magic-link sign-in flow without removing existing behavior. Add /auth/callback to complete the magic-link session, handle errors, and restore the user's intended destination; and preserve existing sign-in, sign-up, and session logic. Never expose service-role or SMTP credentials in frontend code.",v5e="Complete and save the URL and SMTP settings first. AI can generate a compatible authentication flow after the draft is ready.",b5e="Google sign-in",w5e="Let visitors sign in to the generated website with their Google account.",S5e="Loading Google sign-in settings…",_5e="Google sign-in settings couldn't be loaded",C5e="The current provider configuration has not been changed.",I5e="Not configured",E5e="Enabled",T5e="Disabled",P5e="Google provider changes apply directly and may take up to 30 seconds to reach all authentication services. They do not activate or modify the email authentication draft.",k5e="Activate URL settings before enabling Google sign-in",A5e="Google must return users to a configured website URL after authorization. You can save the Client ID and Client Secret now, but Google sign-in cannot be enabled until the URL settings are active.",R5e="Open URL settings",D5e="Waiting for URL activation",x5e="Enable Google sign-in",L5e="Show Google as a sign-in option after the compatible website flow has been published.",O5e="Create OAuth credentials in Google Cloud",N5e="Create a Web application OAuth client and add the exact Supabase Auth callback below as an Authorized redirect URI.",M5e="Open Google Cloud",F5e="Client IDs",j5e="123456.apps.googleusercontent.com, 789012.apps.googleusercontent.com",B5e="Separate multiple Client IDs with commas. 